    {
      "id": "installable-template-instructions",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "Discussion Map",
      "position": {
        "x": -220,
        "y": 700
      },
      "width": 760,
      "height": 300,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 210
        },
        {
          "id": "top",
          "label": "top",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "value",
          "angle": 270
        },
        {
          "id": "right",
          "label": "right",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "value",
          "angle": 0
        },
        {
          "id": "bottom",
          "label": "bottom",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "value",
          "angle": 90
        },
        {
          "id": "left",
          "label": "left",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "value",
          "angle": 180
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "installable-template-capabilities"
        },
        "markdown": "# Discussion Map\n\nUse the semantic edges to follow the proposal:\n\n- the audience **is affected by** whole-graph template ownership\n- that problem **motivates** installable capabilities\n- the proposal **assumes** one root can host bounded behaviors\n- the workboard audit **informs** the open installation-contract question\n- current reconciler behavior **supports** the assumption\n- collision risk **threatens** the idea\n- the proof task **tests** the assumption and **advances** the proposed approach\n\nKeep whole-graph derivation and capability installation as separate authority operations."
      }
    },
